message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the archived version below and the related article."
type: software
title: "resched_lab: closed-loop workbench, data and results for a two-stage fuzzy decision layer for rescheduling in digital-twin-enabled production systems"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-29
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Kalinowski
    given-names: Krzysztof
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7601-2575"
    affiliation: "Silesian University of Technology, Faculty of Mechanical Engineering, Department of Engineering Processes Automation and Integrated Manufacturing Systems, Gliwice, Poland"
    email: krzysztof.kalinowski@polsl.pl
abstract: >-
  Python workbench (OR-Tools CP-SAT) for evaluating rescheduling policies in
  closed loop with a digital-twin emulator: a two-stage fuzzy decision layer
  (whether to act: IGNORE/DEFER/RESCHEDULE; how: right shift, match-up, full
  rescheduling) with decision features computed from digital-twin projections,
  benchmark policies (fixed, threshold, myopic oracle), an illustrative job shop
  and an automated gear-wheel line with 624 operations. Includes input data,
  cached baseline schedules, raw simulation results and verification tests.
keywords:
  - rescheduling
  - digital twin
  - fuzzy logic
  - predictive-reactive scheduling
  - constraint programming
  - production planning
